From 3c3effe76768534a63ebc40d4fe0d6d3fe4f4c97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:33:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui_gateway): an accepted submit survives a client socket
 drop; unanswered messages show as not sent [daveey]

An edited message sent during a Desktop reconnect was saved but never ran: no reply, and agent.log showed
no trace of why (t_ed201037).

Why chain (confirmed against agent.log/gui.log/desktop.log/state.db and reproduced):
1. prompt.submit accepted the edit (history 25 -> 13, user row 583321 persisted) and started the deferred
   agent build for the cold-resumed record.
2. The chat ran on gpt-6-astra/openai-codex all day; at 22:55:37 the Codex OAuth token was gone. With no
   Codex credentials `_make_agent` raises AuthError ("No Codex credentials stored"), so the build failed.
3. The build's failure path and every exit of `_run_after_agent_ready` before `_run_prompt_submit` log
   nothing, so the accepted message read in agent.log as one that never ran. The client only got event
   frames, which the concurrent renderer socket drop (1006 at 22:55:41) can lose.
4. The user switched the chat to claude-opus-5-5 (config.set rebuilt the failed agent); the next message
   ran at once, but the failed one was never re-sent and nothing flagged it as unanswered.
5. Hypothesis "the socket drop abandons the submit" is refuted for a short reconnect (test below), but a
   real drop exists for a longer one: past the 20 s orphan-reap grace, a turn still parked on its agent
   build has no activity clock, so `_ws_orphan_turn_activity_is_fresh` called it wedged, the reaper
   interrupted it, the waiter's cancel branch sent a bare error to the dead socket and the session was
   reaped. Live check on a real `hermes serve`: before, resume came back on a new runtime, idle, no
   inflight, and the message never ran; after, the turn completed.

Fix:
- The orphan reaper treats a turn waiting on a live agent build as fresh (the wait has its own cap).
- Log a failed agent build and every pre-agent exit of the turn thread.
- session.resume (live reattach, cold and deferred) projects an unanswered newest user row as a retained,
  retryable failed turn ("Not sent ...", error_surface runtime/turn_not_started) when no turn is running,
  queued, leased by another process or covered by a crash marker. The Desktop renders it with the
  existing error card and Retry. SessionDB.latest_conversation_tail reads the one row for the deferred
  path.

Tests: tests/tui_gateway/test_submit_survives_reconnect.py (4 fail before, 6 pass after).
---
